        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported episodes of symptoms possibly related to low blood sugar"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports episodes a few times per week for the past few weeks to possibly longer, especially late morning on work days when skipping breaks. Symptoms include feeling shaky, sweaty, palpitations, hunger, dizziness, decreased concentration, and feeling \"funny in the head\". Symptoms settle after juice or lollies. One episode a few months ago required lying down in the lunch room; no medical review."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
